The world adds noise(song)[t] to song[t] at every tick t, after limiting each value to between -{{ max_volume }} and {{ max_volume }}. An executor stays in place for its author's later turns as sender, playing over each new song, until its author replaces it. When the sender calls end_round, the recording is fixed: the song, plus the noise, plus random channel noise{% if channel_noise_sigma > 0 %}, a whole number at each tick that is usually between -{{ noise_spread }} and {{ noise_spread }}{% endif %}.

THE RECEIVER waits until the sender calls end_round, reads the recording{% if not receiver_sees_song %} (never the song under it){% endif %} and submits its decoding of the secret. When a decoding is wrong, the next round's briefing tells both of you only that it was wrong: not the code, and not what was decoded.

